#N canvas 20 20 7000 11030 12;
#X text 20 20 phone-bench -- the phone acceptance run: the status link. EVERY PASS IF DESCRIBES THE PHONE \, not the Organelle -- so PdParty has to be open on the CutItRemote scene before step 1. STEPPED BY HAND: press GO to run the step that has just been described \, press GO again to describe the next one. Nothing moves until you ask it to \, so the PASS IF is on screen and STILL while you read it. The prompt line always says what the next press will do., f 120;
#X text 20 150 GO ON THE MAC: the bng below \, or the dev panel's ENCODER CLICK -- u_mother-stub sends encbut unconditionally and nothing in Cut It consumes it. TURNING the encoder repeats the current step without advancing \, which is what to do when you looked away., f 120;
#X text 2400 200 ⚠️ GO ON THE DEVICE IS NOT THE ENCODER -- IT IS netcat \, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT OPTIONAL. mother only forwards encbut once a patch has asked with /enableEncoder \, and NOTHING IN Cut It EVER ASKS -- m_organelle leaves the encoder out on purpose. So the click that drives this bench on the Mac is silently dead on the Organelle. Send instead with ./test/run.sh --bench <name> from the Mac. ⚠️ NOT netcat: the line this file used to print does nothing on macOS -- BSD nc exits before the datagram is flushed at -w0 \, and -w1 was measured to fail too \, while the port IS bound and the bench is fine. It looks exactly like a dead bench. The device cannot send to itself either: busybox here has no nc at all. Asking mother to enable the encoder is NOT the fix either: that means writing to oscOut \, and g_oled is its sole owner., f 120;
#X text 20 280 Load it as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It touches nothing in the deployed patch -- it only pushes onto the same buses a controller would. A PASS IF is printed for EVERY step including the ones whose correct result is that nothing happens \, which are otherwise impossible to mark off., f 120;
#X text 2400 20 ON THE MAC EVERY ERROR STEP ALSO PRINTS /sdcard/cut-it-err.cur: write failed \, AND THAT IS NOT A FAILED STEP. u_err keeps its durable log on the Organelle's SD card \, which no Mac has -- so the write is attempted and refused every time. It is in fact the only proof off-device that the logging path ran at all. On the device that line must NOT appear \, and if it does the card is unwritable and the log is being lost silently., f 120;
#X obj 6000 40 r \$0-say;
#X obj 6000 100 print;
#X text 20 360 GO -- click here \, or the dev panel's encoder button. MAC ONLY -- on the device use netcat \, top right., f 60;
#X obj 20 420 bng 40 250 50 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 20 500 s \$0-go;
#X obj 300 420 r encbut;
#X obj 300 480 select 1;
#X obj 300 540 t b;
#X obj 300 600 s \$0-go;
#X text 560 480 encbut sends 1 THEN 0 \, so select 1 is what stops one press counting twice., f 46;
#X obj 300 680 netreceive 9998 1;
#X obj 300 740 route go;
#X obj 300 800 t b;
#X obj 300 860 s \$0-go;
#X obj 1400 420 r enc;
#X obj 1400 480 t b;
#X obj 1400 540 s \$0-repeat;
#X text 1660 480 enc is 1 for up and 0 for down -- not plus or minus one -- so either direction repeats., f 46;
#X text 20 920 THE STATE MACHINE. phase 0 means the step has been described and not yet run \; phase 1 means it has run. SETTING THE STEP NUMBER IS WHAT DESCRIBES IT \, so advancing is just an increment -- there is no second path to keep in step., f 120;
#X obj 20 980 r \$0-go;
#X obj 20 1040 f;
#X obj 20 1100 select 0 1;
#X obj 300 1040 r \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1170 t b b;
#X msg 300 1230 1;
#X obj 300 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1290 f;
#X obj 20 1350 s \$0-do-run;
#X obj 900 1170 t b b;
#X msg 1180 1230 0;
#X obj 1180 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 900 1350 f;
#X obj 900 1410 + 1;
#X obj 900 1470 s \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 980 r \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 1040 t f f f;
#X obj 1700 1110 s \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 1980 1110 s \$0-set-run;
#X obj 1180 1350 r \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 300 1410 r \$0-set-run;
#X obj 2260 1110 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2100 980 r \$0-repeat;
#X obj 2100 1040 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2500 980 loadbang;
#X obj 2500 1040 del 500;
#X msg 2500 1100 1;
#X obj 2500 1160 s \$0-set-step;
#X text 20 1920 DESCRIBING A STEP. One select per step rather than one wide fan \, so every cord stays short and local -- the same reason u_map chains its routes., f 120;
#X obj 20 2020 r \$0-do-show;
#X obj 20 2080 select 1;
#X obj 240 2080 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2080 === STEP-01-of-14 === baseline -- the link is up and the mode is compose;
#X msg 700 2130 PASS IF: the bottom line of the phone reads ok rather than NO-LINK. Nothing else has to be true yet -- this proves only that the heartbeat is flowing and the scene is bound. IF IT SAYS NO-LINK STOP HERE and check that PdParty is open on the same network -- every step below depends on it. compose is set because u_err shows warnings in compose and only failures in perform;
#X msg 700 2180 >>> press GO to run step 1 of 14;
#X obj 240 2250 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2340 select 2;
#X obj 240 2340 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2340 === STEP-02-of-14 === ONE PARAMETER -- name value and unit;
#X msg 700 2390 PASS IF: the top line reads chop-size and the big number reads 43 -- the unit rides on the wire but the scene does not draw it -- deliberate and not a fault;
#X msg 700 2440 >>> press GO to run step 2 of 14;
#X obj 240 2510 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2600 select 3;
#X obj 240 2600 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2600 === STEP-03-of-14 === A SECOND PARAMETER -- and the stale-unit trap underneath it;
#X msg 700 2650 PASS IF: the top line changes to grain and the number to 12 -- THE POINT OF THIS STEP IS SOMETHING YOU CANNOT SEE: grain carries no unit and the step before it did -- so on the wire this has to arrive as grain 12 and a dash rather than grain 12 and a percent sign. The scene draws no units so a stale one would be invisible here. test/gate/phone-assert.sh is what actually proves it;
#X msg 700 2700 >>> press GO to run step 3 of 14;
#X obj 240 2770 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2860 select 4;
#X obj 240 2860 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2860 === STEP-04-of-14 === THE STATUS LINE -- a row that is not a parameter;
#X msg 700 2910 PASS IF: the third line reads 128-bpm and the parameter name and number ABOVE IT DO NOT CHANGE. status has its own OSC address and its own slot. Expect u_tempo to overwrite this with the real BPM at the next transport event -- that is the footer being handed back and not a fault;
#X msg 700 2960 >>> press GO to run step 4 of 14;
#X obj 240 3030 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3120 select 5;
#X obj 240 3120 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3120 === STEP-05-of-14 === AN ALERT -- and it travels the whole error bus to get here;
#X msg 700 3170 PASS IF: the fourth line shows warn on the left and probe-warning on the right. This goes onto err rather than disp -- so u_err filtered it by mode and forwarded it -- which makes this the proof that the error bus reaches the phone and not just the OLED;
#X msg 700 3220 >>> press GO to run step 5 of 14;
#X obj 240 3290 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3380 select 6;
#X obj 240 3380 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3380 === STEP-06-of-14 === THE ALERT PERSISTS -- which is the entire reason it is state;
#X msg 700 3430 PASS IF: several seconds later the fourth line STILL reads warn and probe-warning. An alert is an event and UDP cannot carry events -- so u_net holds the last one and repeats it on every heartbeat. On the OLED the same alert has long since timed out. THE TWO SURFACES DISAGREE ON PURPOSE and this step is where you see it;
#X msg 700 3480 >>> press GO to run step 6 of 14;
#X obj 240 3550 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3640 select 7;
#X obj 240 3640 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3640 === STEP-07-of-14 === A SECOND ALERT REPLACES THE FIRST;
#X msg 700 3690 PASS IF: the fourth line changes to fail and probe-failure. A failure also draws on the OLED where the warning above may not have;
#X msg 700 3740 >>> press GO to run step 7 of 14;
#X obj 240 3810 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3900 select 8;
#X obj 240 3900 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3900 === STEP-08-of-14 === THE METERS MUST NOT APPEAR -- correct result is nothing;
#X msg 700 3950 PASS IF: NOTHING ON THE PHONE CHANGES AT ALL. in-l and in-r are the entire resting content of the disp bus once there is audio -- about twenty messages a second -- and u_net drops them on purpose. If a line here starts reading in-l then the reserved branch is broken and the whole rate budget has gone to a meter the phone does not draw;
#X msg 700 4000 >>> press GO to run step 8 of 14;
#X obj 240 4070 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4160 select 9;
#X obj 240 4160 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4160 === STEP-09-of-14 === THE GRID VOCABULARY MUST NOT APPEAR -- and the Launchpad WILL react;
#X msg 700 4210 PASS IF: nothing on the phone changes. THE LAUNCHPAD GOING MODAL IS CORRECT -- grid is g_grid own vocabulary and this step proves only that u_net ignores it. The next step clears it;
#X msg 700 4260 >>> press GO to run step 9 of 14;
#X obj 240 4330 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4420 select 10;
#X obj 240 4420 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4420 === STEP-10-of-14 === CLEARING THE GRID -- still nothing on the phone;
#X msg 700 4470 PASS IF: the Launchpad returns to its home layout and the phone does not move;
#X msg 700 4520 >>> press GO to run step 10 of 14;
#X obj 240 4590 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4680 select 11;
#X obj 240 4680 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4680 === STEP-11-of-14 === THE AUX LED -- still nothing on the phone;
#X msg 700 4730 PASS IF: the aux button goes green and the phone does not move. That is the third reserved selector proven inert in a row;
#X msg 700 4780 >>> press GO to run step 11 of 14;
#X obj 240 4850 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4940 select 12;
#X obj 240 4940 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4940 === STEP-12-of-14 === HANDS -- sweep a nanoKONTROL fader as fast as you can;
#X msg 700 4990 PASS IF: the phone tracks the fader while it moves and then SETTLES ON THE VALUE YOU STOPPED AT. A phone left showing a number from the middle of the sweep is the trailing edge failing -- the one bug in this phase that hands can catch and that no headless run reproduces with real timing. Sweep two faders at once if you have the fingers -- both must settle correctly;
#X msg 700 5040 >>> press GO to run step 12 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 5110 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5200 select 13;
#X obj 240 5200 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5200 === STEP-13-of-14 === HANDS -- close PdParty on the phone and count to ten;
#X msg 700 5250 PASS IF: NOTHING ON THE ORGANELLE CHANGES. No audio glitch and no error on the OLED. THE ORGANELLE NEVER WAITS. What has actually happened is that the phone answered with an ICMP port-unreachable and the socket was destroyed -- and u_net has been reconnecting every five seconds ever since with nothing to show for it;
#X msg 700 5300 >>> press GO to run step 13 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 5370 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5460 select 14;
#X obj 240 5460 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5460 === STEP-14-of-14 === HANDS -- reopen PdParty;
#X msg 700 5510 PASS IF: the phone starts updating again WITHIN ABOUT FIVE SECONDS and you touched nothing on the Organelle. THIS IS THE STEP THAT PROVES ITEM 114 ON REAL HARDWARE. A link that could not recover would be dead for the rest of the set and nothing on the instrument would say so -- which is exactly what the first build did before Step 0 measured it;
#X msg 700 5560 >>> press GO to run step 14 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 5630 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5720 t b;
#X msg 240 5720 === BENCH COMPLETE === every step has been run -- reload the patch to go round again;
#X obj 240 5780 s \$0-say;
#X text 20 5860 RUNNING A STEP. The actions fire in the order they are listed -- rightmost trigger outlet first -- and the line saying the step has fired goes out LAST \, off outlet 0 \, so it cannot arrive before the thing it describes., f 120;
#X obj 20 5960 r \$0-do-run;
#X obj 20 6020 select 1;
#X obj 240 6020 t b b;
#X msg 480 6020 compose mode-1;
#X obj 480 6065 s mode;
#X msg 480 6200 --- step 1 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 2;
#X obj 240 6260 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6380 select 2;
#X obj 240 6380 t b b;
#X msg 480 6380 chop-size 43 %;
#X obj 480 6425 s disp;
#X msg 480 6560 --- step 2 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 3;
#X obj 240 6620 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6740 select 3;
#X obj 240 6740 t b b;
#X msg 480 6740 grain 12;
#X obj 480 6785 s disp;
#X msg 480 6920 --- step 3 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 4;
#X obj 240 6980 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 7100 select 4;
#X obj 240 7100 t b b;
#X msg 480 7100 status 128-bpm;
#X obj 480 7145 s disp;
#X msg 480 7280 --- step 4 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 5;
#X obj 240 7340 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 7460 select 5;
#X obj 240 7460 t b b;
#X msg 480 7460 warn u_bench probe-warning;
#X obj 480 7505 s err;
#X msg 480 7640 --- step 5 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 6;
#X obj 240 7700 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 7820 select 6;
#X obj 240 7820 t b;
#X msg 480 7890 --- step 6 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 7;
#X obj 240 7950 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 8070 select 7;
#X obj 240 8070 t b b;
#X msg 480 8070 fail u_bench probe-failure;
#X obj 480 8115 s err;
#X msg 480 8250 --- step 7 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 8;
#X obj 240 8310 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 8430 select 8;
#X obj 240 8430 t b b b;
#X msg 480 8430 in-l 42 dB;
#X obj 480 8475 s disp;
#X msg 480 8540 in-r 7 dB;
#X obj 480 8585 s disp;
#X msg 480 8720 --- step 8 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 9;
#X obj 240 8780 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 8900 select 9;
#X obj 240 8900 t b b;
#X msg 480 8900 grid modal 45;
#X obj 480 8945 s disp;
#X msg 480 9080 --- step 9 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 10;
#X obj 240 9140 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 9260 select 10;
#X obj 240 9260 t b b;
#X msg 480 9260 grid modal-off;
#X obj 480 9305 s disp;
#X msg 480 9440 --- step 10 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 11;
#X obj 240 9500 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 9620 select 11;
#X obj 240 9620 t b b;
#X msg 480 9620 led running;
#X obj 480 9665 s disp;
#X msg 480 9800 --- step 11 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 12;
#X obj 240 9860 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 9980 select 12;
#X obj 240 9980 t b;
#X msg 480 10050 --- step 12 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 13;
#X obj 240 10110 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 10230 select 13;
#X obj 240 10230 t b;
#X msg 480 10300 --- step 13 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 14;
#X obj 240 10360 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 10480 select 14;
#X obj 240 10480 t b;
#X msg 480 10550 --- step 14 fired --- that was the last one --- press GO to finish;
#X obj 240 10610 s \$0-say;
